  <section id="webinar-invitations" class="ef-section" aria-labelledby="webinar-invitations-title">
    <div class="ef-wrap ef-checklist-layout">
      <div>
        <p class="ef-eyebrow">Before the webinar</p>
        <h2 id="webinar-invitations-title">Invite the people you want in the room.</h2>
        <p class="ef-body-lead">Give us the audience, topic and date. We’ll agree which accounts and roles to call and what makes the session worth their time.</p>
        <ol class="ef-checklist wf-invite-steps">
          <li><span aria-hidden="true">01</span><div><h3>Agree the audience</h3><p>Start with your approved list or agree the target accounts, roles and exclusions with us.</p></div></li>
          <li><span aria-hidden="true">02</span><div><h3>Make the invitation</h3><p>Explain the topic, answer the practical questions and share the approved registration details with people who want them.</p></div></li>
          <li><span aria-hidden="true">03</span><div><h3>Confirm registrations</h3><p>Track who registered and agree when to remind them. Make sure guests have the time zone and joining instructions.</p></div></li>
        </ol>
      </div>
      <figure class="ef-handoff-card wf-invite-example">
        <figcaption class="ef-label">Example webinar invitation call</figcaption>
        <blockquote>“Hi [name], this is [caller] calling on behalf of [company]. We’re running a short session on [specific problem] for [role] on [date]. Is that something your team is working on? I can send you the registration link.”</blockquote>
        <p><strong>If they ask for the link</strong></p>
        <p>Confirm where to send it and what the session covers. Record that they requested the details. Count them as registered when the sign-up appears in your event list.</p>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="webinar-follow-up" class="ef-section ef-paper" aria-labelledby="webinar-follow-up-title">
    <div class="ef-wrap">
      <div class="ef-heading">
        <div>
          <p class="ef-eyebrow">After the webinar</p>
          <h2 id="webinar-follow-up-title">Call webinar leads based on what they did.</h2>
        </div>
        <p>We work from your webinar export and CRM notes. Start with explicit requests, then give attendees and no-shows their own opening and next step.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="ef-situation-grid">
        <article>
          <p class="ef-label">Priority 01</p>
          <h3>Asked to speak to sales</h3>
          <p>Pick up their demo request or question. Confirm the use case, who should attend and what they want from the meeting.</p>
          <div class="ef-situation-action"><strong>Example opening</strong><p>“You asked about [specific topic] during the webinar. What would you like our team to cover if we set up a call?”</p></div>
          <p class="ef-next"><span>Possible next step</span>Book a focused demo or discovery call.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <p class="ef-label">Priority 02</p>
          <h3>Attended the session</h3>
          <p>Ask why the topic mattered. Use a question or poll answer when there’s one on record.</p>
          <div class="ef-situation-action"><strong>Example opening</strong><p>“Thanks for joining the session on [topic]. Was there a particular issue you were hoping it would help you solve?”</p></div>
          <p class="ef-next"><span>Possible next step</span>Arrange a call if they have a relevant need, or send the material they asked for.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <p class="ef-label">Priority 03</p>
          <h3>Registered and missed it</h3>
          <p>Use the fact they registered. Find out what they wanted from the session and offer the approved replay.</p>
          <div class="ef-situation-action"><strong>Example opening</strong><p>“You registered for [webinar]. Would the recording help, or was there a question you were hoping we’d cover?”</p></div>
          <p class="ef-next"><span>Possible next step</span>Send the replay, agree a callback, or book a conversation they want to have.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

