        <h2 id="webinar-handoff-title">Give sales a reason for every booking.</h2>
        <p class="ef-body-lead">A qualified webinar meeting needs a relevant account, the right participant and a purpose the buyer agreed to. We confirm the details and pass the conversation notes to the person running the meeting.</p>
        <p class="ef-specialist">Track registrations, attendance from your platform, and meetings booked and held as separate outcomes. For contacts who need more time, record the agreed follow-up and who owns it.</p>
      </div>
      <article class="ef-handoff-card" aria-labelledby="webinar-handoff-example">
        <div class="ef-sheet-top"><span>CRM handoff</span><span>Example</span></div>
        <h3 id="webinar-handoff-example">An attendee wants to see a workflow.</h3>
        <dl>
          <div><dt>Webinar signal</dt><dd>An operations lead asked how the product handles duplicate CRM records.</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Confirmed need</dt><dd>Their team is preparing a CRM migration and wants to review how duplicates are flagged.</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Agreed meeting</dt><dd>A walkthrough with the product specialist. The buyer plans to invite the CRM administrator.</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Sales handoff</dt><dd>Send the question and agreed meeting time to the account owner. Include what the buyer wants to see first.</dd></div>
        </dl>
        <p class="ef-caption">Illustrative meeting brief. Your campaign uses the qualification criteria and handoff fields you approve.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
